---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {formatGbp, formatStorage} from '../lib/format.js';
import {withBase} from '../lib/paths.js';
import {defaultProfileResult, getLatestSnapshot} from '../lib/snapshots.js';

const snapshot = await getLatestSnapshot();
const {results, date} = snapshot.data;
const {profile} = defaultProfileResult(results);
const external = profile.externalStorage;
---

<Base
  title="Methodology"
  description="How the Mac value index is calculated: formulas, profiles and weights, reservations, Geekbench version and caveats."
  path="methodology/"
>
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p>
    The index answers one question: which Apple silicon Mac gives the most
    development capability per £ in the UK right now, new or refurbished? Every
    figure on this site is calculated in advance from the{' '}
    <a href={withBase('sources/')}>sources</a>. The description below is for the
    snapshot of {date}.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="formulas">
    <h2 id="formulas">Formulas</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Model memory headroom</strong>: RAM minus{' '}
        {profile.reservations.memoryGb} GB.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Usable storage</strong>: SSD minus{' '}
        {profile.reservations.storageGb} GB. 1 TB is counted as 1,000 GB.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Normalisation</strong>: {results.normalisation.description}
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>GPU and bandwidth</strong>: {profile.gpuAndBandwidthSplit.metal}
        % normalised Geekbench Metal score and{' '}
        {profile.gpuAndBandwidthSplit.memoryBandwidth}% normalised memory
        bandwidth.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Capability score</strong> (zero to 100): the sum of each
        normalised metric multiplied by its profile weight.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Value score</strong>: capability score divided by price,
        multiplied by 1,000. This is the ranking key. Ties break on higher
        capability score, then lower price, then listing id.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Pareto frontier</strong>: listings for which no other listing is
        both at least as cheap and at least as capable.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Stable</strong>: in the top 10 under every profile.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>{profile.reservations.assumption}</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="profiles">
    <h2 id="profiles">Profiles and weights</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <caption>Weights by profile. Each row sums to 100.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Profile</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">
              Multi-core
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">
              Memory headroom
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">
              GPU and bandwidth
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">
              Single-core
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">
              Usable storage
            </th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {results.profiles.map(result => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">
                <code>{result.profile.id}</code>
                {result.profile.id === results.defaultProfileId && ' (default)'}
                <br />
                <span class="meta">{result.profile.description}</span>
              </th>
              <td class="num">{result.profile.weights.multiCore}</td>
              <td class="num">{result.profile.weights.memoryHeadroom}</td>
              <td class="num">{result.profile.weights.gpuAndBandwidth}</td>
              <td class="num">{result.profile.weights.singleCore}</td>
              <td class="num">{result.profile.weights.usableStorage}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="floors">
    <h2 id="floors">Floors and model classes</h2>
    <p>
      Listings with less than {profile.floors.minRamGb} GB of RAM or less than{' '}
      {formatStorage(profile.floors.minSsdGb)} of SSD are excluded. A listing is
      also excluded when its chip has no verified benchmark for a weighted
      metric: figures are never estimated.
    </p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <caption>
          Largest local model that fits in the memory headroom at 4-bit
          quantisation
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Model class</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">
              Minimum headroom
            </th>
            <th scope="col">Assumption</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {profile.modelClasses.map(modelClass => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{modelClass.label}</th>
              <td class="num">{modelClass.minHeadroomGb} GB</td>
              <td>{modelClass.assumption}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="benchmarks">
    <h2 id="benchmarks">Benchmarks</h2>
    <p>
      Processing figures are Geekbench {results.geekbenchVersion} single-core,
      multi-core and Metal scores. One Geekbench version is used throughout;
      versions are never mixed. Chip notation such as "12/16-core" means a
      12-core CPU and a 16-core GPU.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="sensitivity">
    <h2 id="sensitivity">Storage sensitivity</h2>
    <p>
      Desktops are also re-scored with a {formatStorage(external.capacityGb)}{' '}
      external SSD added:{' '}
      <a href={external.sourceUrl} rel="noopener">
        {external.product}
      </a>{' '}
      at {formatGbp(external.priceGbp)}, retrieved {external.retrievedDate}. The
      result is in each <a href={withBase('reports/')}>report</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="caveats">
    <h2 id="caveats">Caveats</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Benchmarks measure short synthetic workloads. Sustained performance,
        thermal limits and real build or inference speed can differ.
      </li>
      <li>
        Stock and prices change quickly, especially refurbished stock. Check the
        source listing before buying.
      </li>
      <li>
        Warranty and returns differ between new, Apple refurbished and
        third-party refurbished machines.
      </li>
      <li>
        Desktop prices exclude a display, keyboard and pointing device. Laptop
        prices include them.
      </li>
      <li>
        Colour and display-finish variants of one configuration are collapsed to
        the cheapest.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
